# Confidential and licensed data -- see the data handling section of CLAUDE.md.
#
# Licensed vendor data (IQVIA, Komodo, MarketScan, Symphony/HealthVerity) must never be
# committed: those licences prohibit redistribution and git history is permanent. Real
# asset assumptions are confidential. Only synthetic or public example parameters belong
# in params/ itself.
params/real/

# Source material, held back from the remote pending a redistribution decision.
#
# reference/assumptions_register.xlsx cites Komodo, Merative/MarketScan, IQVIA,
# Symphony, HealthVerity, Truveta and Datavant as the sources behind its Low/Base/High
# values, and names assumption owners. That is the category CLAUDE.md says must never be
# committed. The .jsx, .docx and .pdf carry no vendor names, but travel with it.
#
# Everything needed to run and verify the model is committed: the engine, the priors,
# the Monte Carlo, the tests and the example parameters. Only tests/test_jsx_trace.py
# needs the .jsx present, and it skips cleanly when it is absent.
reference/

